+Example: run evaluations with thresholds in custom code.
+
+```ts
+import { Eval } from 'frai-core';
+
+const dataset = Eval.loadDataset({ outputsPath: 'outputs.json', referencesPath: 'refs.json' });
+const evaluations = Eval.runEvaluations({ outputs: dataset.outputs, references: dataset.references });
+
+// Generate a report with thresholds. Thresholds are optional.
+const report = Eval.generateReport({
+  evaluations,
+  outputsPath: dataset.outputsPath,
+  referencesPath: dataset.referencesPath,
+  thresholds: { exact_match: 0.9, toxicity: 0.95 }  // Optional: set minimum scores
+});
+
+// JSON and Markdown reports both include threshold results.
+Eval.writeReport({ report, format: 'json', reportPath: 'report.json' });
+Eval.writeReport({ report, format: 'markdown', reportPath: 'report.md' });
+
+// Check results in your code
+if (report.passed === false) {
+  console.error('One or more thresholds failed');
+  process.exit(1);
+}
+```
+
 Because `frai-core` is a regular ESM package, you can import only the modules you need and embed FRAI capabilities inside automation pipelines, CI jobs, or custom products.
 
